timestamp=2026-11-09T08:34:55.499Z level=INFO run=d54a47dc message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us think differently: follow the exact rule as stated. Rule 3 says \"it is enclosed in parentheses\" - meaning the entire value/amount is enclosed in parentheses. That’s typically (123.45). So both ( and ) must be present as enclosing characters around the number? That’s the strict interpretation. Also \"contains the token CR\", \"contains a minus sign -\". These are different conditions. So for R00279 '113 , 61 C2) ' it has ) but is not enclosed in () - it just ends with ). So under strict reading, it’s not negative due to parens. That’s important.\n# Same for '113 , 61 C2) ' in the sample: no opening (. So strict parens → not negative. That changes sign.\n# Similarly '(142' has opening but no closing → not enclosed → not negative due to parens. But also has no minus, no CR. So base would be positive +142. But combined with WAIVE=TRUE, net becomes 0 anyway. That’s why it doesn’t matter? Let us test.\npass\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
