timestamp=2026-11-09T08:41:03.770Z level=INFO run=d54a47dc message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Maybe the answer is fine as computed? Let us look at what we got - the result is a list of 10 record_ids. The problem states the answer is the top 10 record_id values in the specified order. Let us also look at one potential issue: when deduplicating, we must \"keep one row per record_id by choosing the latest event_time, breaking ties by preferring the version with a real net result, then earlier file order.\" What counts as \"real net result\"? They said \"preferring the version with a real net result\" - all our net values are finite after filtering? Or maybe they mean not NaN. Also we need to be careful about how we select among duplicates *before* filtering? Or look up the exact sequence.\n# Also: \"keep only rows with non-missing event_time, event_time between ... , channel != \"phone\" (case-insensitive), and finite net, then within each (region, month) group ...\"\n# So filtering happens first (on the cleaned/processed rows). Then deduplication happens after filtering? Or deduplication happens globally on the dataset considering the \"version\" choice? The wording says: \"force net = 0 if waive=true, and keep net=NaN if base_amount is NaN, then, after working out net, keep one row per record_id by choosing...\" So dedup happens after computing net for all rows. Then we filter based on event_time, channel, finite net etc. That order matters.\n# Looking at the exact task text: \"force net = 0 if waive=true, and keep net=NaN if base_amount is NaN, then, after working out net, keep one row per record_id by choosing the latest event_time, breaking ties by preferring the version with a real net result, then earlier file order. Keep only rows with non-missing event_time, ...\" So dedup comes AFTER computing net, and BEFORE filtering by event_time/channel/finite net? Or the filtering happens after dedup? Let us re-read: \"then, after working out net, keep one row per record_id...\" - so deduplication is done at that point. Then \"Keep only rows with non-missing event_time, event_time between ...\" - so filtering happens after deduplication. That means we choose the best version per record_id from ALL rows (including those with missing event_time, phone channel, etc.), then filter. That could change which rows survive. We need to check the order.\npass\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
